From: Vikash Garodia <vikash.garodia@oss.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250: Reserve low IOVA range for Venus

Source: https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/08/07/632
Message-ID: 20260807-iris_iova_600mb_fix-v1-21-3996f67e33f9@oss.qualcomm.com
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 13:55:05 +0530

Venus reserves low IOVA for non-pixel buffers. Prevent ordinary DMA
allocations from using the same range. This reserves virtual I/O addresses,
not an additional 600 MiB of physical RAM.

Signed-off-by: Vikash Garodia <vikash.garodia@oss.qualcomm.com>
Backport note: insertion context adapted to the reserved-memory layout in
apollo-7.1.0-r12; reservation and consumer values are unchanged.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
@@ -866,6 +866,17 @@
 			reg = <0x0 0x8bf00000 0x0 0x4600000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * The Venus VPU reserves IOVA below 0x25800000 (600MB),
+		 * primarily for non-pixel buffers using different Stream IDs.
+		 * DMA into that range triggers unhandled SMMU faults and
+		 * spontaneous reboots, so reserve it to keep IOMMU
+		 * allocations above this boundary.
+		 */
+		venus_iova: venus-iova {
+			iommu-addresses = <&venus 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x25800000>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	smem {
@@ -4386,7 +4397,7 @@
 			interconnect-names = "cpu-cfg", "video-mem";
 
 			iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x2100 0x0400>;
-			memory-region = <&video_mem>;
+			memory-region = <&video_mem>, <&venus_iova>;
 
 			resets = <&gcc GCC_VIDEO_AXI0_CLK_ARES>,
 				 <&videocc VIDEO_CC_MVS0C_CLK_ARES>;
